" :ID: property creation (org#id#set) on top of org#core#set_property.

Execute (new drawer after planning lines, Emacs spacing):
  new | setfiletype org
  call setline(1, ['* TODO Task', '  SCHEDULED: <2026-07-01 mié>'])
  call org#id#set()
  AssertEqual '  :PROPERTIES:', getline(3)
  Assert getline(4) =~# '^  :ID:       [0-9a-f-]\{36}$', getline(4)
  AssertEqual '  :END:', getline(5)
  bwipeout!

Given org (existing drawer is reused, even after :LOGBOOK:):
  * Task
  :LOGBOOK:
  - Note taken on [2026-01-01 jue 10:00]
  :END:
  :PROPERTIES:
  :CATEGORY: home
  :END:

Execute:
  call org#id#set()

Then:
  AssertEqual 8, line('$')
  AssertEqual ':CATEGORY: home', getline(6)
  Assert getline(7) =~# '^:ID:       \S\+$', getline(7)

Given org (an existing ID is left alone):
  * Task
  :PROPERTIES:
  :ID:       abc-123
  :END:

Execute:
  call org#id#set()

Expect org:
  * Task
  :PROPERTIES:
  :ID:       abc-123
  :END:

Given org (set_property replaces a value in place, keeping indent):
  * Task
    :PROPERTIES:
    :EFFORT:   1:00
    :END:

Execute:
  call org#core#set_property(1, 'EFFORT', '2:30')
  call org#core#set_property(1, 'LAST_REPEAT', '[2026-01-01 jue 10:00]')

Expect org:
  * Task
    :PROPERTIES:
    :EFFORT:   2:30
    :LAST_REPEAT: [2026-01-01 jue 10:00]
    :END:
